+### authorize(...)
+
+```typescript
+authorize(options?: AuthorizeOptions | undefined) => Promise<AuthorizeResult>
+```
+
+Get an access token for the `scopes` given to `initialize()`,
+without signing in again.
+
+Unlike `signIn()`, this only requests authorization: it does not show
+the sign-in sheet or return an ID token. Once the user has granted the
+scopes, it returns a fresh access token with no UI.
+
+With `interactive: false`, no UI is ever shown: the call rejects with
+the `NEEDS_INTERACTION` error code when the user must consent first.
+
+On Web, a token can't be obtained without a redirect, so
+`interactive: false` always rejects with `NEEDS_INTERACTION`, and
+`interactive: true` redirects as `signIn()` does: complete it with
+`handleRedirectCallback()`, whose result carries the access token.
